WEBVTT

00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:20.650
Don't be afraid.

00:00:20.650 --> 00:00:23.100
I'm God, you see!

00:00:23.100 --> 00:00:24.480
What is that thing?

00:00:24.480 --> 00:00:26.650
And this smell...

00:00:26.650 --> 00:00:30.900
God my ass!

00:00:30.900 --> 00:00:33.310
You said you wouldn't do any--

00:00:33.310 --> 00:00:34.730
You runaway brat.

00:00:34.730 --> 00:00:37.310
You ignorant fools!

00:00:37.310 --> 00:00:40.190
The great principal of
capitalism is give-and-take.

00:00:40.190 --> 00:00:44.770
There's no such thing as give-and-give!

00:00:46.650 --> 00:00:48.270
I am God.

00:00:48.270 --> 00:00:50.940
Love is me.

00:00:50.940 --> 00:00:53.060
You came looking for love,

00:00:53.060 --> 00:00:56.150
and yet you reject me?

00:00:54.100 --> 00:00:55.570
Don't act on your own.

00:00:56.150 --> 00:00:57.060
Sorry.

00:00:57.060 --> 00:01:01.770
I physically can't stand his looks or his smell.

00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:05.230
It's always hard to understand
how you girls think.

00:01:05.230 --> 00:01:07.810
But we agree on that, at least.

00:01:16.810 --> 00:01:18.520
Come to me.

00:01:18.520 --> 00:01:21.190
I know you haven't gone far.

00:01:21.190 --> 00:01:25.650
Even back then, you only went
one subway stop from home.

00:01:25.650 --> 00:01:27.850
You got scared and ran back home,

00:01:27.850 --> 00:01:31.270
but there was no place for you there, was there?

00:01:31.270 --> 00:01:33.230
Your parents don't love you.

00:01:33.230 --> 00:01:36.600
I'm the only one who will.

00:01:36.600 --> 00:01:40.100
When you ran away,
weren't you saved for a moment?

00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:42.480
That was blowing off steam.

00:01:42.480 --> 00:01:45.310
That's the kind of relationship
you should have built.

00:01:45.310 --> 00:01:46.900
You must understand.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:50.980
Let's blow off each other's steam.

00:01:50.980 --> 00:01:52.730
I'll blow it off for you.

00:02:16.560 --> 00:02:18.650
I'm going

00:02:18.650 --> 00:02:21.850
to blow your mind.

00:02:21.850 --> 00:02:23.270
My...

00:02:27.150 --> 00:02:28.650
Oh, wow!

00:02:28.650 --> 00:02:31.350
But why's his mind down there?

00:02:31.350 --> 00:02:34.310
Nothing I eat will taste right for a while.

00:02:37.310 --> 00:02:38.650
Thank you.

00:02:38.650 --> 00:02:40.850
I didn't do it for you.

00:02:40.850 --> 00:02:44.150
Give-and-give would just be gross.

00:02:44.150 --> 00:02:45.980
I guess so.

00:02:45.980 --> 00:02:47.690
But it made me happy.

00:02:47.690 --> 00:02:49.730
Having somebody protect me.

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.810
Is that so?

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:08.910
Wonder Egg Priority

00:04:29.310 --> 00:04:30.940
We're a little late.

00:04:29.450 --> 00:04:34.960
Episode 5: 'The Girl Flautist'

00:04:30.940 --> 00:04:33.060
This place is hard to find.

00:04:33.060 --> 00:04:34.520
Not so loud.

00:04:38.650 --> 00:04:39.730
You got lost?

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:41.810
No.

00:04:41.810 --> 00:04:44.690
Oh, here.

00:04:44.690 --> 00:04:46.270
For you.

00:04:46.270 --> 00:04:47.850
Thanks.

00:04:49.810 --> 00:04:53.650
Come in! It's cramped, though.

00:04:49.930 --> 00:04:55.440
Ohto

00:04:53.650 --> 00:04:56.270
Excuse us!

00:04:56.270 --> 00:04:57.730
I'm Neiru Aonuma.

00:04:57.730 --> 00:04:59.900
Oh, my, how polite.

00:04:59.900 --> 00:05:01.440
Hi, Ai's Mom.

00:05:01.440 --> 00:05:02.560
My.

00:05:02.560 --> 00:05:03.400
Hello.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:06.850
Oh, my! Aren't you Mr. Sawaki's...?

00:05:08.190 --> 00:05:10.690
Momoe Sawaki. I'm his niece.

00:05:10.690 --> 00:05:12.600
What a pretty young lady.

00:05:12.600 --> 00:05:13.690
Th--

00:05:13.690 --> 00:05:15.940
Hey, do you have that cake?

00:05:15.940 --> 00:05:17.810
Lay out Neiru's snacks, too.

00:05:17.810 --> 00:05:19.400
Fine, fine.

00:05:19.400 --> 00:05:22.560
You have so many friends.

00:05:22.560 --> 00:05:25.810
Isn't that great, Ai?

00:05:25.810 --> 00:05:27.150
Hey!

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:29.650
Please, please, please!

00:05:29.650 --> 00:05:31.900
You really are shameless.

00:05:31.900 --> 00:05:33.730
You haven't even finished yours.

00:05:33.730 --> 00:05:34.770
Stingy.

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.020
Now, now.

00:05:36.020 --> 00:05:39.900
Still, you're really my uncle's student, Ai?

00:05:39.900 --> 00:05:43.270
I hear he's crazy popular
with the girls at school.

00:05:43.270 --> 00:05:44.730
Makes sense.

00:05:44.730 --> 00:05:47.900
If you were a guy, I'd want to date you.

00:05:47.900 --> 00:05:48.980
Stop that.

00:05:48.980 --> 00:05:51.980
I think Koito liked Mr. Sawaki, too.

00:05:51.980 --> 00:05:53.270
Who's Koito?

00:05:53.270 --> 00:05:55.980
The girl Ai's trying to save.

00:05:55.980 --> 00:05:58.270
Oh, I see.

00:05:58.270 --> 00:05:59.440
Oh.

00:05:59.440 --> 00:06:01.650
I just had a crazy idea.

00:06:01.650 --> 00:06:03.350
What? What is it?

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:08.980
Okay, I'll tell you.

00:06:08.980 --> 00:06:12.810
Maybe Ai's best friend Koito
was actually dating Mr. Sawaki.

00:06:12.810 --> 00:06:15.650
Then, something terrible happened, and...

00:06:17.730 --> 00:06:19.900
Oh? Do you have company?

00:06:19.900 --> 00:06:22.810
We do. Ai's friends are here!

00:06:20.350 --> 00:06:22.810
W-Wait a minute!

00:06:22.810 --> 00:06:25.150
My uncle's not like that.

00:06:25.150 --> 00:06:29.060
He's so nice that he adopts lots of rescue cats.

00:06:29.060 --> 00:06:31.520
Maybe he just likes cats.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:34.230
He might have a dark side.

00:06:32.620 --> 00:06:34.370
Ai's Room

00:06:34.650 --> 00:06:36.150
Yeah!

00:06:36.150 --> 00:06:38.690
A teacher got hands on with a student,

00:06:38.690 --> 00:06:42.440
and when it got dicey, bam! Just like that.

00:06:42.440 --> 00:06:43.770
There's no way.

00:06:43.770 --> 00:06:45.060
Maybe she got pregnant.

00:06:45.060 --> 00:06:46.060
Pregnant?!

00:06:46.060 --> 00:06:47.150
Pregnant.

00:06:47.150 --> 00:06:50.060
Yeah, pregnant.

00:06:50.060 --> 00:06:51.690
Give it a rest!

00:06:53.310 --> 00:06:55.400
S-Sorry.

00:06:55.400 --> 00:06:57.770
I was kidding.

00:06:57.770 --> 00:06:59.730
Sorry.

00:07:01.190 --> 00:07:06.730
I really don't know why Koito died.

00:07:06.730 --> 00:07:08.060
So...

00:07:11.350 --> 00:07:13.850
Why not ask your mom?

00:07:13.850 --> 00:07:16.980
Maybe Mr. Sawaki told her something.

00:07:16.980 --> 00:07:19.900
Hey, maybe he only checks on you every week

00:07:19.900 --> 00:07:24.940
because he thinks you've got some kind of proof.

00:07:24.940 --> 00:07:27.400
That could be it, right?

00:07:27.400 --> 00:07:28.850
I can't ask.

00:07:28.850 --> 00:07:34.350
My mom really trusts Mr. Sawaki,
and I'm always making her worry.

00:07:34.350 --> 00:07:39.600
And she stopped asking about my injuries
after I clammed up about them.

00:07:39.600 --> 00:07:41.560
"Clammed," huh?

00:07:44.520 --> 00:07:45.900
What?

00:07:45.900 --> 00:07:47.650
You got allergies?

00:07:47.650 --> 00:07:52.100
No, it's just that I can picture Ai as a clam.

00:07:52.100 --> 00:07:54.190
I-I mean...

00:07:54.190 --> 00:07:58.150
But if you tell her you're
going out to fight in your sleep,

00:07:58.150 --> 00:07:59.980
you'll just worry her more.

00:07:59.980 --> 00:08:02.100
She might think you're on something.

00:08:02.100 --> 00:08:04.770
She'd never believe you.

00:08:04.770 --> 00:08:06.230
Yes.

00:08:06.230 --> 00:08:08.520
That's why we can't tell anyone.

00:08:08.520 --> 00:08:13.520
It's our story that no one else
knows about, right?

00:08:13.520 --> 00:08:17.850
A story... that no one knows about.

00:08:18.940 --> 00:08:20.270
Momoe's here?

00:08:20.270 --> 00:08:23.770
Yes, I recognized her
because she looks like you.

00:08:23.770 --> 00:08:26.900
They're in different schools.
Where did they meet?

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:32.900
There's no reason to have a complex.

00:08:32.900 --> 00:08:35.850
Your eyes are charming.

00:08:35.850 --> 00:08:37.480
Okay.

00:08:37.480 --> 00:08:40.900
I'll paint how you look to me.

00:08:40.900 --> 00:08:44.770
When it's finished, I want you
to have confidence.

00:08:45.940 --> 00:08:47.730
Me, confident?

00:08:47.730 --> 00:08:51.690
I hear Mr. Sawaki's entering it
in the next exhibition.

00:08:51.690 --> 00:08:56.060
He says he want to win a prize
and make a living as a painter.

00:08:56.060 --> 00:08:57.560
A painting of me?

00:08:57.560 --> 00:08:59.400
Confident?

00:08:59.400 --> 00:09:01.980
If not, you should decline.

00:09:01.980 --> 00:09:05.400
Mr. Sawaki's future is on the line.

00:09:05.400 --> 00:09:06.850
I...

00:09:15.350 --> 00:09:18.810
I wish my mom was more like yours, Ai.

00:09:18.810 --> 00:09:21.230
Why? What's yours like?

00:09:21.230 --> 00:09:23.480
Mine's toxic and awful.

00:09:23.480 --> 00:09:27.060
I bet when I was born
and first saw her face, I thought,

00:09:27.060 --> 00:09:31.150
"This lady wants to stay a woman
her whole life and never be a parent."

00:09:31.150 --> 00:09:34.400
"Oh, no! What do I do?"

00:09:34.400 --> 00:09:36.020
It's your turn, Rika.

00:09:36.020 --> 00:09:41.190
My mom always does everything
perfectly, at work and at home.

00:09:41.190 --> 00:09:43.350
She works really hard.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:47.600
But I think that's probably why my dad left.

00:09:47.600 --> 00:09:50.810
Lots of guys are proud.

00:09:50.810 --> 00:09:53.690
A capable woman actually spoils them.

00:09:53.690 --> 00:09:55.310
Why are you looking at me?

00:09:55.310 --> 00:09:57.940
Because it's your turn.

00:09:57.940 --> 00:10:00.850
You're an anachronistic fool.

00:10:00.850 --> 00:10:02.310
Who are you calling "fool"?

00:10:02.310 --> 00:10:03.730
Stop, fool.

00:10:05.020 --> 00:10:07.150
Coochy-coochy-coo...

00:10:07.150 --> 00:10:08.900
How about here?

00:10:10.400 --> 00:10:12.230
They really get along, huh?

00:10:12.230 --> 00:10:13.270
Yeah.

00:10:13.270 --> 00:10:14.650
No, we--

00:10:14.650 --> 00:10:17.520
What about this spot?

00:10:23.600 --> 00:10:24.770
Hey,

00:10:24.770 --> 00:10:27.230
do you do hair treatments?

00:10:27.230 --> 00:10:29.900
It looks like you've got some damage.

00:10:29.900 --> 00:10:33.270
Don't touch me.

00:10:33.270 --> 00:10:37.850
I want to be free. Don't tie me down.

00:10:37.850 --> 00:10:39.350
Oh, who cares?

00:10:39.350 --> 00:10:42.440
Hey, isn't my hair pretty?

00:10:42.440 --> 00:10:44.270
Not a single split end.

00:10:44.270 --> 00:10:46.310
I'm at my prettiest now.

00:10:46.310 --> 00:10:48.940
Nothing can replace youth.

00:10:48.940 --> 00:10:50.230
Not interested.

00:10:50.230 --> 00:10:55.350
Aren't you going to ask? About why I died?

00:10:55.350 --> 00:10:58.310
I just complete my objectives.

00:10:58.310 --> 00:10:59.770
Get back!

00:11:05.900 --> 00:11:08.350
Girls become adults.

00:11:08.350 --> 00:11:12.020
The miraculous beauty of a butterfly emerging.

00:11:12.020 --> 00:11:13.810
A brief moment.

00:11:13.810 --> 00:11:19.270
A moment of shocking beauty when
its transience is powerfully reflected.

00:11:19.270 --> 00:11:20.730
Mirror, mirror on the wall,

00:11:20.730 --> 00:11:24.020
who's the fairest of them all?

00:11:28.560 --> 00:11:32.770
Soon, beauty fades.

00:11:32.770 --> 00:11:34.940
My mom's just a sow.

00:11:34.940 --> 00:11:38.600
No amount of liposuction or hyaluronic acid

00:11:38.600 --> 00:11:40.400
will ever stop her aging.

00:11:40.400 --> 00:11:45.560
In fact, her attempts to stop it
are unbelievably ugly on their own.

00:11:45.560 --> 00:11:49.060
You're pretty, too. Why don't you die?

00:11:49.060 --> 00:11:51.600
Why not die when you're at your most beautiful?

00:11:51.600 --> 00:11:54.190
Why cling to a meaningless life?

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:54.190
This isn't good.

00:11:54.190 --> 00:12:08.940
Mirror, mirror on the wall,
who's the fairest of them all?

00:11:56.230 --> 00:11:57.810
How do I beat them?

00:11:57.810 --> 00:12:01.770
Hey, why don't you die?

00:12:01.770 --> 00:12:03.600
Why don't you?

00:12:03.600 --> 00:12:08.940
Tell me!

00:12:09.950 --> 00:12:11.710
Near the station's south exit: Model homes on display

00:12:10.400 --> 00:12:11.980
Okay, coast's clear.

00:12:11.980 --> 00:12:14.650
The crosswalk is right there.

00:12:14.650 --> 00:12:17.310
Who wants to wait?

00:12:17.310 --> 00:12:19.980
You have a lot, huh, Momo?

00:12:19.980 --> 00:12:22.770
Yeah, a bunch, actually.

00:12:24.650 --> 00:12:25.850
Be quiet, Rika.

00:12:25.850 --> 00:12:27.060
Yay!

00:12:27.060 --> 00:12:27.900
Ai!

00:12:27.900 --> 00:12:29.650
Hey, there's an echo.

00:12:29.650 --> 00:12:32.600
I wonder what they grew here.

00:12:32.600 --> 00:12:34.900
That reminds me; I'm starving.

